From 03c77d7eba8571cc6627198becf25f53e06201a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iPhone crash and hang reports through MetricKit reach the
 owner, no SDK, no account (rule 1760)

The app subscribes to MXMetricManager at launch and posts a compact summary of each
MXDiagnosticPayload (crash, hang, CPU, disk, launch) to POST /api/app-diagnostics:
version, build, OS, device model, exception, signal, termination reason, up to 30
"binary +offset" frames and a count. No account id, no user content.

The route needs no sign-in, is rate limited per address (app-diagnostics, 12/hour),
caps the body at 32 KB and 10 reports, and keeps only well-formed system strings.
Reports go to the errlog as ios-<kind> (alert: false), an ios-diag:<kind> day counter
the daily ops digest now shows, and a crash alerts the owner once per new
(version, exception, top frame) signature per UTC day.

DEBUG builds: a long press on Settings' colophon shows a developer row that writes a
MetricKit signpost and posts a sample report. Privacy page, privacy manifest (Crash Data,
Performance Data, not linked), IOS.md App Store answers, API and SECURITY docs updated.
Swift not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
